# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the host KV tier SHIP-CANDIDATE gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-tier-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TCX1 (STOP): EXACTNESS of the ship candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-traffic (the control plus the host tier at its production setting: QWEN_PREFIX_HOST_TIER_GIB=32, verify=sample, audit=0, and the
# preconverted checkpoints) against its control TCX0 on the same image: the same prompts, unaudited; a traffic profile under the candidate's OWN owner traffic waiver (id w2-er-fx-tier-262k-2026-10-11, decision PENDING: it boots in a smoke
# and logs the word). READ: python3 scripts/ci/parked_compare.py --control <TCX0 smoke log> --parked <TCX1 smoke log> --control-container <TCX0 container log> --parked-container <TCX1 container log>
# --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-traffic: every levern_equal, levern_equal_busy and parked_equal content hash EQUAL, compared above 0, the parked judge with 0 problems under the lever band; and in the TCX1 container log the
# lines 'host tier IO attached' and 'host tier on gib=32.00 ... verify=sample audit=0' and no 'latched off' line (c2_smoke_check has no tier rule: read them by hand). The smoke forces no eviction, so the tier restores
# nothing here: this job proves that the ATTACHED tier leaves the exactness list as it was. The restore's own exactness is TC1 (the restored answer against its cold twin) and the seven seats' text is the
# cross-arm comparison of TC2 to TC5. Any difference is NO-GO. The ARC telemetry sidecar (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py) samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current, temperature, kernel NOPs); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and reads only. Duration (estimate): 25 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,parked_equal,parked_budgets,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=exactness tier arm: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
C2_TELEMETRY=1
